{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The maximum magnitude outcome for both lotteries is 1000 Euros (in Lottery B, it occurs with 50% probability; in Lottery A, the only outcome is 500 Euros, so its maximum magnitude outcome is 500 Euros). The reason evaluates which lottery has the more favorable maximum magnitude outcome weighted by its probability. For Lottery A, this is 500 (100% × 500). For Lottery B, it is 1000 × 50% = 500. Thus, both lotteries have the same weighted maximum magnitude outcome (500), so the reason would be indifferent between them, or possibly prefer B if only the raw maximum outcome (1000) is considered as more favorable despite equal weighting. The relevant information (maximum outcomes and their probabilities) is available in the problem.",
